# 2. PRIMARY PROBLEM TO SOLVE

The current implementation is substantially functional, but the overall product experience is not yet coherent enough.

The most important problem is the journey from:

```text
ROOT
 ↓
SIGN UP / SIGN IN
 ↓
PHONE
 ↓
OTP
 ↓
ACCOUNT CREATION
 ↓
ROLE / INTENT
 ↓
ONBOARDING
 ↓
HOME
 ↓
ROLE-SPECIFIC EXPERIENCE
```

The current mobile and web implementations do not yet provide one clearly defined, coherent identity and onboarding model.

The product needs a single, understandable mental model.

The user should never be confused about:

* whether they are signing up or signing in
* what happens after OTP verification
* why they are being asked for a role
* whether selecting a role is permanent
* whether they can have multiple roles
* what onboarding remains incomplete
* whether they are a tenant, landlord, agent, property manager, etc.
* why they are seeing a particular home/dashboard
* whether mobile and web represent the same account
* which application they should use for a particular task
* what they are currently operating as
* what they are authorized to do

