# 6. DO NOT START WITH UI

The first goal is to establish the canonical product state machine.

Define the user's lifecycle.

At minimum, investigate whether the following states are required:

```text
UNKNOWN
 ↓
PHONE_E
NTERED
 ↓
OTP_SENT
 ↓
PHONE_VERIFIED
 ↓
ACCOUNT_CREATED
 ↓
ONBOARDING_REQUIRED
 ↓
ONBOARDING_IN_PROGRESS
 ↓
ONBOARDING_COMPLETE
 ↓
AUTHENTICATED
```

But do not blindly implement this exact model.

Determine the correct state machine from the existing architecture.

The critical requirement is:

> Authentication state and onboarding state must be separate concepts.

A user can be:

```text
authenticated
```

but still:

```text
onboarding_incomplete
```

A user can also be:

```text
authenticated
+
tenant role
+
landlord role
+
identity verification pending
```

Those states must not be collapsed into one boolean.

