# 7. DESIGN THE CANONICAL AUTHENTICATION FLOW

Determine and implement one canonical flow.

The desired conceptual flow is:

```text
APP ROOT
   ↓
Do we have a valid session?
   │
   ├── NO
   │    ↓
   │  Enter phone
   │    ↓
   │  OTP
   │    ↓
   │  Verify
   │
   └── YES
        ↓
     Load current user
        ↓
     Determine account state
        ↓
     Determine onboarding state
        ↓
     Determine available roles
        ↓
     Determine current context
        ↓
     Route appropriately
```

There must NOT be arbitrary client-side routing based solely on assumptions such as:

```text
new user → role
existing user → home
authenticated web user → properties
```

The backend should provide enough state for clients to make the correct routing decision.

